# Aiven CA certificate (placeholder)

# This file is read by server.js (cloudSslOptions) and
# server/config/dbEndpoints.js (buildEndpoint) only when DB_SSL=true.
#
# NOTE: rejectUnauthorized is already set to false in the SSL config,
# so the CA certificate content is NOT used for verification. The server
# will start and connect successfully regardless of this file content.
#
# To replace with the real Aiven CA certificate:
#   1. Go to https://console.aiven.io -> your MySQL service -> Overview
#   2. Copy the "CA certificate" (PEM format) from the connection details
#   3. Paste it below, replacing this placeholder
#
# The real certificate looks like:
# -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
# <base64-encoded certificate data>
# -----END CERTIFICATE-----

